Package: tabfound
Title: Tabular Foundation Models in Pure R Torch
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Marcel", "Neunhoeffer",
           email = "marcel@marcel-neunhoeffer.com",
           role  = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Inference-only R implementations of open-weight tabular
    foundation models (TabPFN v2.5 to v3.5, TabICL, TabFM, Mitra) on top of
    the 'torch' package, with no Python runtime at fit or predict time. A
    formula interface handles factors, dates, text and missing values, and
    returns tidy predictions, including predictive quantiles. The models'
    predictive distributions also drive multiple imputation (interoperating
    with 'mice' and 'Amelia') and sequential synthetic data generation
    (interoperating with 'synthpop'). Each model's network, preprocessing
    and ensembling are verified against its reference Python implementation.
